From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: JiaY-shi <shi05275@163.com>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 23:40:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] net: pcs: mtk-lynxi: cache link advertisement

The downstream MT7988 platform driver reconfigures the PCS from
pcs_link_up() without an advertisement mask.  This is safe for SGMII, but
phylink_mii_c22_pcs_encode_advertisement() dereferences the mask for
1000BASE-X and 2500BASE-X.  The GL-MT2500 therefore crashes when its
2500BASE-X link comes up.

Cache the advertisement supplied by phylink and reuse it for internal
reconfiguration, as done by the newer OpenWrt version of this driver.

Fixes: 524164f5839f ("net: pcs: pcs-mtk-lynxi: add platform driver for MT7988")
Signed-off-by: JiaY-shi <shi05275@163.com>
---
 drivers/net/pcs/pcs-mtk-lynxi.c | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/pcs/pcs-mtk-lynxi.c b/drivers/net/pcs/pcs-mtk-lynxi.c
index 51a31bbe8fcc..f657134efb89 100644
--- a/drivers/net/pcs/pcs-mtk-lynxi.c
+++ b/drivers/net/pcs/pcs-mtk-lynxi.c
@@ -94,6 +94,7 @@ struct mtk_pcs_lynxi {
 	struct device		*dev;
 	u32			ana_rgc3;
 	phy_interface_t		interface;
+	__ETHTOOL_DECLARE_LINK_MODE_MASK(advertising);
 	struct			phylink_pcs pcs;
 	u32			flags;
 	struct fwnode_handle	*fwnode;
@@ -204,8 +205,11 @@ static int mtk_pcs_lynxi_config(struct phylink_pcs *pcs, unsigned int neg_mode,
 	int advertise, link_timer;
 	int ret;
 
+	if (advertising)
+		linkmode_copy(mpcs->advertising, advertising);
+
 	advertise = phylink_mii_c22_pcs_encode_advertisement(interface,
-							     advertising);
+							     mpcs->advertising);
 	if (advertise < 0)
 		return advertise;
 
